    "single-original": "EDIT TARGET: the attached approved game character illustration. Remove ONLY the cream paper background, border, caption, Roman numeral and any ground shadow outside the subject. Return a true transparent RGBA cutout. Preserve the complete character, its exact pose, faceted geometric illustration style, face, hair, clothing colors, hammer, ruler and beige display base. Do not add, redraw, relight, recolor, mirror, simplify or change any equipment. Keep the original square canvas and original subject position and scale; retain clean detailed edges and transparent holes between body and tools. No new text, checkerboard, gray backdrop, glow or cast shadow. This is background removal of gallery reference artwork, not a render of a 3D model.",
    "single-front": "EDIT TARGET: the attached gallery reference artwork. Remove the cream/white paper background, all borders, separators, text, captions, numbers and any shadows OUTSIDE each subject. Return genuinely transparent RGBA. Preserve every character's recognizable approved identity, exact pose, equipment, face, colors, faceted geometric illustration style, magical particles and beige display base. Do not relight, recolor, mirror or redesign. Do not add a checkerboard, gray backdrop, outline, glow or new text. If the input is a multiview sheet, extract ONLY the complete FRONT figure in the TOP LEFT panel as one large centered portrait. Discard every other view and detail panel. If it is already one illustration, retain the entire subject. Fit the entire subject including weapons and pedestal inside a square transparent canvas with a small even margin.",
    "atlas": "EDIT TARGET: the attached gallery reference artwork. Remove the cream/white paper background, all borders, separators, text, captions, numbers and any shadows OUTSIDE each subject. Return genuinely transparent RGBA. Preserve every character's recognizable approved identity, exact pose, equipment, face, colors, faceted geometric illustration style, magical particles and beige display base. Do not relight, recolor, mirror or redesign. Do not add a checkerboard, gray backdrop, outline, glow or new text. This is a CHARACTER ATLAS. KEEP THE ENTIRE SHEET'S EXACT ORIGINAL ASPECT RATIO, GRID, SUBJECT COUNT, POSITIONS, SIZES AND CELL ORDER. Do not rearrange, enlarge, merge or omit any subjects. Make the original paper and grid transparent in place. Every character stays in its original cell, fully intact, at its original relative position. Transparent holes between equipment and limbs. The output will be cropped at the original cell coordinates."
